# Project dependency compatibility

Status: incomplete inactive seed. Complete and independently review this
project-owned document and `.engineering-backbone/dependencies.json` before
activation. Existing local requirements remain binding. Copier preserves this
file during updates; it does not infer a stack or install a Dockerfile.

Read [the shared dependency policy](../.engineering-backbone/dependency-policy.md)
and [navigation guide](../.engineering-backbone/navigation-guide.md).

For each actual component, record:

- Component ID and kind (`application`, `library` or `tooling`), matching its
  navigation/dependency configuration.
- Authoritative manifest, resolution, runtime and Dockerfile paths. These must be
  real tracked files; reference their versions rather than copying package lists.
- Supported runtime, package manager, toolchain, platforms and coupled versions.
  Libraries also explain supported ranges and their reproducible test environment.
- Clean installation and manifest/resolution/declared-requirement checks; actual
  PR `dependency`, `build`, `test` and, for Dockerfiles, `container` check IDs.
- Behavioral compatibility matrix, meaningful integration coverage, native target
  and PostgreSQL evidence where applicable; record unexecuted or unsupported cases.
- Update ownership, review/migration scope, evidence location and recovery approach.

Ensure this document and all declared inputs are covered by the corresponding
navigation component's literal paths. Complete the inactive contract first, then
activate it in a separate enabled-only PR with the matching reviewed workflow pin.
